        "slc_c6cfb88390989a8d61ff2ff504fbdf4bfe491eea21dcb2fb4503b5f4fca4d043"
      ],
      "text": "HALO is described as a methodology for building recursively self-improving agent harnesses using RLMs, with the repo containing a desktop app, methodology docs, a Python engine package, and demos."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_7df3a5dbdf9586bcc6b93014c53bdce9205c527e0f92a5f6efce6638c00bbef7",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "specifications",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "b7f8509745d67b499b4e80efe20ea37c03426a74",
          "git_sha": "d4b2f346439a76976a0182e5773875d5156a8df0",
          "line_end": 142,
          "line_start": 138,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "context-labs/halo",
          "url": "https://github.com/context-labs/HALO/blob/b7f8509745d67b499b4e80efe20ea37c03426a74/README.md#L138-L142"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_e7561cd440080af4f6001e46fbe883943c916d19638720413360b1d3d9bcaca8"
      ],
      "text": "The HALO loop: collect OpenTelemetry-compatible traces from an agent harness, feed them to the HALO-RLM engine, which decomposes traces into common failure modes and produces a report that a coding agent turns into harness changes, then the cycle repeats."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_d539bc03b6fc4b52f2c80abc382ed3c484755af10320f5dce1a14a17e618e5f6",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "design-choices",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "b7f8509745d67b499b4e80efe20ea37c03426a74",
          "git_sha": "d4b2f346439a76976a0182e5773875d5156a8df0",
          "line_end": 148,
          "line_start": 148,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "context-labs/halo",
          "url": "https://github.com/context-labs/HALO/blob/b7f8509745d67b499b4e80efe20ea37c03426a74/README.md#L148-L148"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_3e918f3e635780a77fec78f642d2c2b8ef81d4a97355bbb1e469bfb62ba52509"
      ],
      "text": "The authors argue general harnesses like Claude Code overfit to errors in single traces when analyzing long traces, motivating a specialized RLM for systemic trace analysis."
    },
